5)  a #polymorph command.  Why isn't there a way to #polymorph
>    oneself, once one has a ring of polymorph control?  Also, why
>    not have intrinsic polymorph if one eats a dead shape-changer
>    or is bitten by one(vampire bites (in either direction) could
>    give one a semi-permanent polymorph to vampire).
  Once bitten by a vampire you should be able to polymorph into either a 
VAMPIRE, BAT or WOLF, and maybe even mimic other undead creatures.  As
the victim of a vampire, the only way to be transformed back into human
form would be to drink holy water, or some other holy act.  Vampires 
should be afraid of lit rooms, so therefore vampires should be able
to see in the dark.  Also vampires should need to feed on live pray.
Whenever a vampire is hungry and hits a creature, an option should be 
made to the player to bite the creature, which should in turn lead to the 
imediate death of that creature.  I would think that a hungry vampire
would be a very playable character.



